WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.208 --> 00:00:01.884
- Welcome to London!

00:00:01.884 --> 00:00:03.492
We're from Canada we can handle it.

00:00:03.492 --> 00:00:08.363
Nina, don't die on your
first day in London, okay?

00:00:08.363 --> 00:00:10.946
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.892 --> 00:00:26.225
Day...

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:27.058
one.

00:00:30.268 --> 00:00:32.451
We got off the plane.

00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:34.032
How'd you do, Nina?

00:00:34.032 --> 00:00:35.365
How'd you sleep?

00:00:36.656 --> 00:00:38.152
- Slept, a couple, few hours.

00:00:38.152 --> 00:00:39.114
- [Evan] That's not bad.

00:00:39.114 --> 00:00:41.620
Nina's seat wasn't working properly.

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:43.023
Didn't go down. But they fixed it?

00:00:43.023 --> 00:00:44.088
They had to do it manually?

00:00:44.088 --> 00:00:45.136
- They had to do it manually.

00:00:45.136 --> 00:00:46.479
- But you still were able to sleep?

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.557
- Yeah.

00:00:47.557 --> 00:00:49.057
- Then we had a...

00:00:50.317 --> 00:00:52.900
medical emergency on the plane.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.607
They were calling for a doctor but,

00:00:56.607 --> 00:00:59.866
nobody said yes. So
they had an ambulance...

00:00:59.866 --> 00:01:00.757
Anyway.

00:01:00.757 --> 00:01:04.843
We got off. We're going
to go through customs.

00:01:04.843 --> 00:01:08.565
And then head on the Tube. The
subway in London is the Tube.

00:01:08.565 --> 00:01:11.171
I don't think I slept, I rested.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.670
I don't think I slept at all.

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:13.891
I rested.

00:01:13.891 --> 00:01:15.391
Welcome to London!

00:01:16.329 --> 00:01:18.996
(calming music)

00:01:22.518 --> 00:01:25.677
How's that London air, Nina?

00:01:25.677 --> 00:01:27.251
Feels good, actually.

00:01:27.251 --> 00:01:29.139
A little chilly, but...

00:01:29.139 --> 00:01:32.056
We're from Canada we can handle it.

00:01:34.489 --> 00:01:36.167
- Ceiling's low.

00:01:36.167 --> 00:01:37.000
- [Evan] Ceiling's low?

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:37.833
- Yeah.

00:01:37.833 --> 00:01:38.682
- [Evan] Well, you're pretty low.

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:40.450
- No, I was thinking of you.

00:01:40.450 --> 00:01:42.186
- Thinking of me? I'm
going to hit my head?

00:01:42.186 --> 00:01:44.826
Actually, it does look like
I'm going to hit my head.

00:01:44.826 --> 00:01:47.291
It's okay, it's just big enough.

00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:49.867
England can't handle Evan.

00:01:49.867 --> 00:01:51.162
I like the music they play.

00:01:51.162 --> 00:01:52.827
Oh, there's a guy here that's why.

00:01:52.827 --> 00:01:57.196
I thought they were playing
it on the sound speaker.

00:01:57.196 --> 00:01:59.460
- McDonalds, they have chocolate McFlurry.

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:01.346
- [Evan] You want a chocolate McFlurry?

00:02:01.346 --> 00:02:03.308
Are you already thinking about food, Nina?

00:02:03.308 --> 00:02:04.141
- It's different.

00:02:04.141 --> 00:02:05.001
- [Evan] Different food in London

00:02:05.001 --> 00:02:06.570
and you want to go to McDonald's.

00:02:06.570 --> 00:02:08.534
That's what I used to always do.

00:02:08.534 --> 00:02:10.096
Anytime I went to a new city
I would go to McDonald's

00:02:10.096 --> 00:02:11.162
and they would make fun of me.

00:02:11.162 --> 00:02:12.495
So, inside joke.

00:02:14.892 --> 00:02:16.283
How's the weather feel?

00:02:16.283 --> 00:02:18.250
- Cool.
- Refreshing, huh?

00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:21.833
Nice! Alright, time to
explore some London.

00:02:24.624 --> 00:02:27.228
So, we officially know where we're going.

00:02:27.228 --> 00:02:28.573
Nina's our tour guide.

00:02:28.573 --> 00:02:30.313
- No, I don't know what I'm doing.

00:02:30.313 --> 00:02:31.191
- I'm the tour guide.

00:02:31.191 --> 00:02:33.733
We're going to hit, we're
going to go find our hotel

00:02:33.733 --> 00:02:35.199
which is just past Trafalgar Square

00:02:35.199 --> 00:02:38.803
which is one of the most
popular areas in London.

00:02:38.803 --> 00:02:41.733
Drop off our bags, change.

00:02:41.733 --> 00:02:44.453
A little bit on the smelly side, perhaps.

00:02:44.453 --> 00:02:45.286
- You.

00:02:46.717 --> 00:02:48.550
- Both of us. I think.

00:02:49.858 --> 00:02:51.608
Oh! Nina, food. Look!

00:02:52.817 --> 00:02:56.209
And today's going to be
our exploring and shopping

00:02:56.209 --> 00:03:00.899
and vibrant area city day.
Once we drop our stuff off.

00:03:00.899 --> 00:03:02.057
Let's go!

00:03:02.057 --> 00:03:05.135
The iconic British telephone booth.

00:03:05.135 --> 00:03:08.685
I wonder how much longer
they're going to be around.

00:03:08.685 --> 00:03:10.829
You guys spot the Canada flag?

00:03:10.829 --> 00:03:13.148
Can you see the Canada flag?

00:03:13.148 --> 00:03:15.015
Here's a clue.

00:03:15.015 --> 00:03:18.288
Boom. Look at that. Canadian
Embassy, straight ahead.

00:03:18.288 --> 00:03:22.455
We're not going there though,
we're going to get our hotel.

00:03:25.768 --> 00:03:29.377
Nina's discovered some food.
What do you want to eat?

00:03:29.377 --> 00:03:30.707
- Lemon tart.

00:03:30.707 --> 00:03:32.439
- [Evan] You want to eat all of that Nina?

00:03:32.439 --> 00:03:34.029
Remember, we're going on a cruise ship.

00:03:34.029 --> 00:03:34.862
- [Nina] Yeah.

00:03:34.862 --> 00:03:39.029
- [Evan] You're going to have
tons of food on the cruise ship.

00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:45.576
Alright, we made it in.

00:03:46.523 --> 00:03:49.713
We got to unpack, we got to
get rid of this heavy bag.

00:03:49.713 --> 00:03:53.856
Oh, yeah! That feels good!
- Your back is sweating.

00:03:53.856 --> 00:03:56.181
- I've been carrying lots of stuff.

00:03:56.181 --> 00:03:58.938
It's only home for one day.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:01.167
We leave tomorrow for the cruise.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:02.838
We got to make the most of today.

00:04:02.838 --> 00:04:04.806
Get changed and hustle,
Nina. Are you ready?

00:04:04.806 --> 00:04:05.639
- Mmhmm.

00:04:05.639 --> 00:04:07.970
- High five? Oh, okay good.

00:04:07.970 --> 00:04:09.142
I thought she was going
to leave me hanging.

00:04:09.142 --> 00:04:11.915
She almost left me
hanging. I love you Nina.

00:04:11.915 --> 00:04:14.416
You guys know when I travel,
you know when I travel

00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:17.083
I need to find CNN. Where's CNN?

00:04:19.423 --> 00:04:22.673
Ah! Nina? We're officially on vacation.

00:04:25.639 --> 00:04:26.472
CNN is on.

00:04:29.432 --> 00:04:31.126
Alright, guys. It's official.

00:04:31.126 --> 00:04:33.513
It's officially on 'cause I got the shirt.

00:04:33.513 --> 00:04:34.919
'Cause we got the shirt.

00:04:34.919 --> 00:04:35.966
How you feeling Nina?

00:04:35.966 --> 00:04:36.799
- Good.

00:04:36.799 --> 00:04:40.210
- Nina wants to hug it
out. Aww hug it out Nina.

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:44.191
Time to go explore. Nina wants
some food. I want some food.

00:04:44.191 --> 00:04:45.409
I want a coffee, actually.

00:04:45.409 --> 00:04:46.639
- Yeah, me too. I want a coffee.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:49.310
- Yeah, I want a coffee. I
want a coffee and some food.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:51.679
It's time to explore! We're finally here!

00:04:51.679 --> 00:04:55.262
Nina's in a new country
and we are excited.

00:04:57.877 --> 00:05:00.591
We're here at Trafalgar Square.

00:05:00.591 --> 00:05:02.113
At the fountain behind us

00:05:02.113 --> 00:05:04.555
some demonstration is happening too.

00:05:04.555 --> 00:05:07.521
So, the Iranian protest is behind us.

00:05:07.521 --> 00:05:11.688
And now there's a vegetarian
protest in front of us.

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.900
(crowd noise)

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.483
(police siren)

00:05:18.887 --> 00:05:22.677
This is the place to have a protest.

00:05:22.677 --> 00:05:25.427
(crowd chanting)

00:05:33.398 --> 00:05:35.974
Nina, we didn't make our
way across before it,

00:05:35.974 --> 00:05:37.508
before it started.

00:05:37.508 --> 00:05:40.008
We didn't make our way across.

00:05:41.361 --> 00:05:43.422
What we want to do is get to that...

00:05:43.422 --> 00:05:45.463
there's a coffee shop on the other side.

00:05:45.463 --> 00:05:48.358
(chuckling) I don't know that
we're going to get through this.

00:05:48.358 --> 00:05:50.754
We're going to go through.
Nina, lead the way.

00:05:50.754 --> 00:05:52.556
(crowd yelling)

00:05:52.556 --> 00:05:56.723
Nina. Nina. Don't die on your
first day in London, okay?

00:05:59.860 --> 00:06:01.027
- Your friend.

00:06:01.885 --> 00:06:02.866
- [Protestor] My name's Jacob.

00:06:02.866 --> 00:06:03.699
- [Evan] Jacob.

00:06:03.699 --> 00:06:06.366
(crowd yelling)

00:06:09.661 --> 00:06:13.828
Oh, nice! Okay, nice! Cool man!
Fan of the channel, alright.

00:06:14.871 --> 00:06:15.704
Did he stop you?

00:06:15.704 --> 00:06:17.712
- Yeah, he said "Nina!".
- Nina.

00:06:17.712 --> 00:06:19.554
- He said, "What's Evan doing here?"

00:06:19.554 --> 00:06:22.595
He's a fan of the channel,
alright. Okay, good.

00:06:22.595 --> 00:06:26.095
Nina's a celebrity, she's recognized here.

00:06:27.286 --> 00:06:30.119
(soft rock music)

00:06:30.957 --> 00:06:34.957
Alright, our destination.
Let's get some coffee.

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:39.473
- It's strong.

00:06:39.473 --> 00:06:40.920
- Alright, you like it strong.

00:06:40.920 --> 00:06:43.369
So, that was the first
time Nina got stopped.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:45.395
Is that the first time
you've been stopped?

00:06:45.395 --> 00:06:47.492
- Huh, like, actually asked, "Nina?"

00:06:47.492 --> 00:06:50.720
- Yeah. And got stopped before me.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:54.720
So, Nina's kicking up her
celebrity profile here

00:06:55.681 --> 00:07:00.200
in London. Look out friends.
Nina's on a warpath.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:03.117
I got to, I got to be your bodyguard.

00:07:04.614 --> 00:07:08.326
Ooh, yum. I like it. Alright!
Exploration continues.

00:07:08.326 --> 00:07:11.113
The chaos is pretty much over behind us.

00:07:11.113 --> 00:07:15.280
The vegan festival march and
now we're going to move on.

00:07:16.890 --> 00:07:18.084
See what we can find.

00:07:18.084 --> 00:07:20.834
So this is the Iranian gathering.

00:07:21.695 --> 00:07:24.246
It's a lot more peaceful than the vegans.

00:07:24.246 --> 00:07:28.005
A lot less yelling. They're
just watching a message on TV.

00:07:28.005 --> 00:07:29.422
Oh, look at this.

00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.930
Guy's doing street art.

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:38.346
I don't know what they're saying but,

00:07:38.346 --> 00:07:41.659
something about death penalty in Iran.

00:07:41.659 --> 00:07:44.607
So, this is the place to
come to make a statement.

00:07:44.607 --> 00:07:47.610
I feel like we need an
entrepreneur rally next.

00:07:47.610 --> 00:07:51.379
Trafalgar Square. Entrepreneurs stand up!

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:54.546
(gentle guitar music)

00:07:57.965 --> 00:08:00.535
oh, that's Shakespeare.
William Shakespeare.

00:08:00.535 --> 00:08:02.195
Did you read Shakespeare in school?

00:08:02.195 --> 00:08:03.028
- Yeah.

00:08:03.967 --> 00:08:05.693
- You memorized everything?
- No, nothing.

00:08:05.693 --> 00:08:07.184
- To be or not to be.
That is the question.

00:08:07.184 --> 00:08:08.267
- Yeah, okay.

00:08:09.303 --> 00:08:11.751
- [Evan] We doing a selfie now?

00:08:11.751 --> 00:08:14.168
- It's pretty cool that
it takes it by yourself,

00:08:14.168 --> 00:08:15.330
automatically.

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:18.929
- [Evan] It's what's called a selfie.

00:08:18.929 --> 00:08:20.859
- I don't have to press a button, okay.

00:08:20.859 --> 00:08:24.015
- [Evan] (laughing) I'm just
teasing you. We love you Nina!

00:08:24.015 --> 00:08:26.015
Nina. Nina. We love you.

00:08:27.936 --> 00:08:30.436
(beat boxing)

00:08:35.803 --> 00:08:40.254
Nina, there's Chinatown. Every
big city has a Chinatown.

00:08:40.254 --> 00:08:42.694
You curious? You want to
go? Nina wants to go, okay.

00:08:42.694 --> 00:08:45.611
Here we go, lets hit the Chinatown.

00:08:50.864 --> 00:08:53.110
What's special about the Golden Phoenix?

00:08:53.110 --> 00:08:56.193
- We have a Phoenix in, um, in, um...

00:08:57.808 --> 00:08:59.353
In Markham too.

00:08:59.353 --> 00:09:01.322
- [Evan] Oh.
- Gerrard Street.

00:09:01.322 --> 00:09:03.301
- [Evan] That's what we're
on. This is Gerrard street.

00:09:03.301 --> 00:09:06.649
- That's uh, we have a
Gerrard Street in Toronto.

00:09:06.649 --> 00:09:09.585
- [Evan] Yeah, a lot of the
streets will be similar names.

00:09:09.585 --> 00:09:12.028
Young Street, Young Street?
I don't know, actually.

00:09:12.028 --> 00:09:13.751
King Street, Queen Street.

00:09:13.751 --> 00:09:15.268
(loud music)

00:09:15.268 --> 00:09:17.768
Nice! Chinese National Anthem.

00:09:20.284 --> 00:09:21.534
Chinese anthem.

00:09:24.989 --> 00:09:27.489
(piano music)

00:09:39.241 --> 00:09:41.639
We're stopping to get
some food. Nina's hungry.

00:09:41.639 --> 00:09:43.999
The sandwich arrived. Nina is starving.

00:09:43.999 --> 00:09:47.582
So she's not even waiting.
She kind of got hangry.

00:09:47.582 --> 00:09:50.377
But here we go, how is it Nina?

00:09:50.377 --> 00:09:52.045
We should leave Nina
alone for a few minutes,

00:09:52.045 --> 00:09:55.545
let her get some food in her. That's cool.

00:09:56.874 --> 00:09:59.874
(soft techno music)

00:10:05.191 --> 00:10:07.174
We're going into Foyles bookstore.

00:10:07.174 --> 00:10:11.341
We're going to see if they have
my book. Nina's already inside.

00:10:12.323 --> 00:10:17.235
So, Foyles is the most
iconic bookstore in London.

00:10:17.235 --> 00:10:18.815
It's been around for over 100 years.

00:10:18.815 --> 00:10:23.229
They have six different
stories of books and gifts

00:10:23.229 --> 00:10:27.151
and a lot of the North American stores,

00:10:27.151 --> 00:10:30.696
